# AbroadKart
## CRM Platform — Data & Infrastructure Specification
**Internal Architecture Document** | **Version 1.0** | **July 2026**

---

### Purpose
This document defines all data entities, fields, and relationships required to build the AbroadKart CRM system for students abroad consultancies.

---

### 1. Overview
AbroadKart CRM is purpose-built for students abroad consultancies. It manages the full lifecycle of a student — from first contact through counselling, document collection, university application, visa filing, and final enrolment.

The system is structured around 7 core entities:

| # | Entity | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 1 | Student (Lead/Contact) | Master record for every prospective student |
| 2 | Interaction / Activity Log | Every touchpoint — calls, WhatsApp, emails, meetings |
| 3 | Application | University applications filed on behalf of the student |
| 4 | Document Checklist | Status tracking for all required documents |
| 5 | Payments / Fees | Consultancy fees, commissions, and invoices |
| 6 | Counsellor / Staff | Internal team members and their assignments |
| 7 | University Master | Reference data for universities worldwide |

---

### 2. Entity: Student (Lead / Contact)
The Student entity is the core of the CRM. Every other entity links back to it. A student enters as a lead and progresses through stages until enrolment or drop-off.

#### 2.1 Identity & Contact
* **id** — Unique identifier
* **name** — Full name
* **email** — Primary email
* **phone** — WhatsApp-preferred mobile number
* **city, state, country_of_origin** — Current location
* **dob** — Date of birth
* **gender**
* **source** — How they found AbroadKart — Reddit, Instagram, Referral, Walk-in, Google, etc.

#### 2.2 Academic Background
* **highest_qualification** — 10th / 12th / UG / PG
* **stream** — Science / Commerce / Arts / Engineering / etc.
* **subjects** — Relevant subjects studied
* **percentage / cgpa** — Academic score
* **backlog_count** — Number of backlogs (if any)
* **year_of_passing**
* **institution_name** — Last attended college or school

#### 2.3 English & Standardised Test Scores
* **ielts_score** — Overall band score
* **toefl_score**
* **pte_score**
* **duolingo_score**
* **gre_score** — For US/Canada PG applicants
* **gmat_score** — For MBA applicants
* **sat_score** — For UG US applicants
* **test_appearing_date** — If test not yet taken

#### 2.4 Work Experience
* **work_experience_years** — Total years of professional experience
* **employer** — Current or most recent employer
* **designation** — Job title
* **gap_explanation** — If there is an education or employment gap

#### 2.5 Study Abroad Goals
* **target_countries[ ]** — Array: UK, Canada, Australia, Germany, USA, Ireland, etc.
* **target_courses[ ]** — Array of preferred course names
* **study_level** — Undergraduate / Postgraduate / PhD / Diploma / Certificate
* **preferred_intake** — January / May / September
* **target_year** — E.g. 2025, 2026

#### 2.6 Financial Profile
* **budget_tuition** — Annual tuition budget (in USD / GBP / CAD)
* **budget_living** — Annual living expense budget
* **funding_type** — Self-funded / Education loan / Scholarship / Parents
* **loan_pre_approved** — Boolean — has bank pre-approved a loan?

#### 2.7 Visa & Travel History
* **prior_visa_refusals** — Boolean — critical for application strategy
* **refusal_countries[ ]** — Which countries refused
* **refusal_reason** — Free text explanation
* **passport_available** — Boolean
* **passport_expiry** — Date

#### 2.8 CRM Status Fields
* **lead_stage** — New → Contacted → Counselled → Docs Collection → Applied → Visa → Enrolled → Lost
* **assigned_counsellor_id** — FK to Counsellor entity
* **priority** — Hot / Warm / Cold
* **lost_reason** — Why the student dropped off (if applicable)
* **created_at, updated_at** — Timestamps

