### 4. Entity: Interaction / Activity Log
Every touchpoint with a student must be logged. This is the audit trail of all CRM activity and the primary source of accountability for counsellors.

* **id** — Unique identifier
* **student_id** — FK to Student
* **counsellor_id** — FK to Counsellor who made contact
* **type** — Call / WhatsApp / Email / In-person Meeting / Reddit / Walk-in
* **direction** — Inbound (student reached out) / Outbound (we reached out)
* **notes** — Free-text summary of the interaction
* **next_action** — What needs to happen next
* **next_action_date** — Follow-up due date
* **created_at** — Timestamp

---

### 5. Entity: Application
A student can have multiple applications — to different universities or intakes. Each is tracked independently.

* **id** — Unique identifier
* **student_id** — FK to Student
* **university_name** — Name of the institution
* **country** — Country of the university
* **course** — Course name
* **level** — UG / PG / PhD / Diploma
* **intake_month, intake_year** — E.g. September 2025
* **status** — Draft / Submitted / Under Review / Offer Received / Conditional / Rejected / Accepted / Deferred
* **offer_letter_url** — Link to uploaded offer letter
* **conditional_requirements** — Any conditions attached to the offer
* **tuition_fee** — Offered tuition fee per year
* **scholarship_awarded** — Amount of scholarship if any
* **applied_on** — Date application was submitted
* **decision_date** — Date university responded

---

### 6. Entity: Document Checklist
Each student has a checklist of documents needed for applications and visa. Status is tracked per document.

* **id** — Unique identifier
* **student_id** — FK to Student
* **application_id** — FK to Application (optional — some docs are student-level)
* **doc_type** — SOP / LOR / Transcript / Mark Sheet / Bank Statement / Passport / IELTS Score Card / CV / Visa Form / Photo / etc.
* **status** — Pending / Received / Verified / Uploaded to Portal / Rejected
* **file_url** — Cloud storage link
* **remarks** — Counsellor notes on the document
* **due_date** — When this document must be ready

---

### 7. Entity: Payments / Fees
Tracks all financial transactions between the consultancy and the student.

* **id** — Unique identifier
* **student_id** — FK to Student
* **fee_type** — Consultation Fee / Application Fee / Visa Filing Fee / Commission / Misc
* **amount** — Amount charged
* **currency** — INR / USD / GBP / CAD / AUD
* **payment_status** — Pending / Partial / Paid
* **payment_date** — Date of payment
* **payment_method** — Cash / UPI / Bank Transfer / Card
* **invoice_url** — Link to generated invoice

---

### 8. Entity: Counsellor / Staff
Internal team members who manage student relationships. Role-based access control should be implemented on top of this entity.

* **id** — Unique identifier
* **name** — Full name
* **email** — Work email (used for login)
* **phone** — Mobile number
* **role** — Admin / Senior Counsellor / Counsellor / Visa Specialist / Document Executive
* **assigned_students[ ]** — Array of student IDs currently assigned
* **specialization_countries[ ]** — E.g. [UK, Canada] — countries they specialise in

---

### 9. Entity: University Master
Reference data for all universities the consultancy works with. Used to auto-populate application fields and filter matches for students.

* **id** — Unique identifier
* **name** — Full university name
* **country, city** — Location
* **ranking** — QS / THE / national ranking
* **popular_courses[ ]** — Top courses this university is known for
* **intake_months[ ]** — Available intakes — e.g. [January, September]
* **tuition_range_min, tuition_range_max** — Annual tuition in USD
* **acceptance_rate** — Percentage
* **min_ielts** — Minimum IELTS band required
* **min_cgpa** — Minimum academic score required
* **application_fee** — In USD
* **application_portal_url** — Direct link to their application portal

